# (slug, era, dates, nameEn, nameCy, epiEn, epiCy, bioEn, bioCy, wikiTitle, after_slug, moreEn, moreCy)
PEOPLE_MORE = [
 ("illtud","ancient","fl. early 6th century","Illtud","Illtud","Teacher of saints","Athro’r seintiau",
  "Founded a monastery and school at Llanilltud Fawr in the Vale of Glamorgan, said to be the first great centre of learning in Britain.",
  "Sefydlodd fynachlog ac ysgol yn Llanilltud Fawr ym Mro Morgannwg, y dywedir mai hi oedd canolfan ddysg fawr gyntaf Prydain.","Illtud","dewi-sant",
  "Later lives of the saints say his pupils included Samson of Dol, Paul Aurelian and Gildas, who spread the faith to Cornwall and Brittany. Carved stones from the early church still stand in St Illtud’s Church at Llantwit Major.",
  "Dywed bucheddau diweddarach y saint fod ei ddisgyblion yn cynnwys Samson o Dol, Pawl Aurelian a Gildas, a ledaenodd y ffydd i Gernyw a Llydaw. Mae cerrig cerfiedig o’r eglwys gynnar yn dal i sefyll yn Eglwys Sant Illtud yn Llanilltud Fawr."),
 ("maelgwn-gwynedd","ancient","d. c. 547","Maelgwn Gwynedd","Maelgwn Gwynedd","The dragon of the island","Draig yr ynys",
  "King of Gwynedd and the most powerful ruler in sixth-century Britain, with his court at Deganwy.",
  "Brenin Gwynedd a rheolwr mwyaf grymus Prydain yn y chweched ganrif, gyda’i lys yn Negannwy.","Maelgwn_Gwynedd","caratacus",
  "The monk Gildas attacked him as a sinner who had killed his way to power, yet also praised his learning. Legend says he won his throne by staying seated on a chair on the sands while rivals floated away on the tide, and that he died of the yellow plague in a church at Rhos.",
  "Ymosododd y mynach Gildas arno fel pechadur a laddodd ei ffordd i rym, ond canmolodd ei ddysg hefyd. Yn ôl y chwedl, enillodd ei orsedd drwy aros yn eistedd ar gadair ar y traeth tra bo’i wrthwynebwyr yn arnofio i ffwrdd ar y llanw, a bu farw o’r fad felen mewn eglwys yn Rhos."),
 ("asser","medieval","d. c. 909","Asser","Asser","Alfred’s Welsh scholar","Ysgolhaig Cymreig Alffred",
  "A monk of St Davids who became adviser to Alfred the Great and wrote the first biography of an English king.",
  "Mynach o Dyddewi a ddaeth yn gynghorydd i Alffred Fawr ac a ysgrifennodd y cofiant cyntaf i frenin o Sais.","Asser","rhodri-mawr",
  "Alfred invited him to Wessex around 885 to help revive learning. Asser agreed to spend half of each year with the king, partly so that St Davids would gain Alfred’s protection. He later became Bishop of Sherborne.",
  "Gwahoddodd Alffred ef i Wessex tua 885 i helpu i adfywio dysg. Cytunodd Asser i dreulio hanner pob blwyddyn gyda’r brenin, yn rhannol fel y câi Tyddewi nawdd Alffred. Yn ddiweddarach daeth yn Esgob Sherborne."),
 ("gruffudd-ap-cynan","medieval","c. 1055–1137","Gruffudd ap Cynan","Gruffudd ap Cynan","King of Gwynedd","Brenin Gwynedd",
  "Born in exile in Dublin, he fought for decades to win Gwynedd and ruled it in peace for his last thirty years.",
  "Fe’i ganed yn alltud yn Nulyn, ac ymladdodd am ddegawdau i ennill Gwynedd a’i rheoli mewn heddwch am ei ddeng mlynedd ar hugain olaf.","Gruffudd_ap_Cynan","gruffudd-ap-llywelyn",
  "He won the Battle of Mynydd Carn in 1081, was captured by the Normans and spent years in prison in Chester before escaping. A Latin life written soon after his death, later translated into Welsh, is the only medieval biography of a Welsh ruler.",
  "Enillodd Frwydr Mynydd Carn yn 1081, cafodd ei ddal gan y Normaniaid a threuliodd flynyddoedd yng ngharchar yng Nghaer cyn dianc. Mae buchedd Ladin a ysgrifennwyd yn fuan ar ôl ei farw, ac a gyfieithwyd yn ddiweddarach i’r Gymraeg, yn unig gofiant canoloesol i reolwr o Gymro."),
 ("nest","medieval","c. 1085–c. 1136","Nest ferch Rhys","Nest ferch Rhys","Princess of Deheubarth","Tywysoges Deheubarth",
  "Daughter of Rhys ap Tewdwr, whose abduction from Cenarth Bychan in 1109 set south Wales alight.",
  "Merch Rhys ap Tewdwr. Pan gipiwyd hi o Genarth Bychan yn 1109, cododd de Cymru yn wenfflam.","Nest_ferch_Rhys","gwenllian",
  "Married to the Norman castellan Gerald of Windsor, she was carried off by Owain ap Cadwgan of Powys. Her many children founded families on both sides of the Welsh and Norman divide, and her grandson was Gerald of Wales.",
  "Yn briod â’r castellydd Normanaidd Gerallt o Windsor, fe’i cipiwyd gan Owain ap Cadwgan o Bowys. Sefydlodd ei phlant niferus deuluoedd ar ddwy ochr y ffin rhwng Cymro a Norman, a’i hŵyr oedd Gerallt Gymro."),
 ("owain-gwynedd","medieval","c. 1100–1170","Owain Gwynedd","Owain Gwynedd","King of Gwynedd, first Prince of the Welsh","Brenin Gwynedd, Tywysog cyntaf y Cymry",
  "King of Gwynedd and son of Gruffudd ap Cynan, who turned back Henry II in 1165 and was the first to call himself Prince of the Welsh.",
  "Brenin Gwynedd a mab Gruffudd ap Cynan, a drodd Harri’r Ail yn ôl yn 1165 ac a fu’r cyntaf i’w alw ei hun yn Dywysog y Cymry.","Owain_Gwynedd","gwenllian",
  "He pushed his border east to the Dee and wrote to the King of France as ‘Prince of the Welsh’. He was excommunicated for marrying his cousin, but was buried in Bangor Cathedral all the same. Legend says his son Madog sailed west and found America.",
  "Gwthiodd ei ffin i’r dwyrain at afon Dyfrdwy ac ysgrifennodd at Frenin Ffrainc fel ‘Tywysog y Cymry’. Cafodd ei esgymuno am briodi ei gyfnither, ond fe’i claddwyd yn Eglwys Gadeiriol Bangor serch hynny. Yn ôl y chwedl, hwyliodd ei fab Madog i’r gorllewin a darganfod America."),
 ("siwan","medieval","c. 1191–1237","Joan, Lady of Wales","Siwan","Princess and peacemaker","Tywysoges a heddychwraig",
  "Daughter of King John of England and wife of Llywelyn Fawr, she often negotiated between Wales and England.",
  "Merch y Brenin John o Loegr a gwraig Llywelyn Fawr, a fu’n aml yn cyfryngu rhwng Cymru a Lloegr.","Joan,_Lady_of_Wales","llywelyn-fawr",
  "In 1230 Llywelyn found her with the Norman lord William de Braose and had him hanged. She was later forgiven, and on her death Llywelyn founded a friary at Llanfaes in her memory. Saunders Lewis made her story into the play ‘Siwan’.",
  "Yn 1230 daliodd Llywelyn hi gyda’r arglwydd Normanaidd Gwilym Brewys a chrogwyd ef. Fe’i maddeuwyd yn ddiweddarach, ac ar ei marwolaeth sefydlodd Llywelyn frodordy yn Llan-faes er cof amdani. Gwnaeth Saunders Lewis ei stori’n ddrama, ‘Siwan’."),
 ("guto-r-glyn","medieval","c. 1435–c. 1493","Guto’r Glyn","Guto’r Glyn","Poet of the gentry","Bardd yr uchelwyr",
  "One of the greatest of the Poets of the Nobility, who praised patrons across Wales in strict-metre verse.",
  "Un o fawrion Beirdd yr Uchelwyr, a ganodd fawl i noddwyr ledled Cymru yn y mesurau caeth.","Guto%27r_Glyn","owain-glyndwr",
  "A soldier in his youth, he fought in France and wrote about the Wars of the Roses. More than 120 of his poems survive. He spent his last years, blind, as a guest of the abbey of Valle Crucis near Llangollen.",
  "Yn filwr yn ei ieuenctid, ymladdodd yn Ffrainc ac ysgrifennodd am Ryfeloedd y Rhosynnau. Mae dros 120 o’i gerddi wedi goroesi. Treuliodd ei flynyddoedd olaf, yn ddall, yn westai yn abaty Glyn y Groes ger Llangollen."),
 ("edward-lhuyd","industrial","1660–1709","Edward Lhuyd","Edward Lhuyd","Naturalist and linguist","Naturiaethwr ac ieithydd",
  "Keeper of the Ashmolean Museum in Oxford, who travelled Wales, Cornwall, Brittany, Ireland and Scotland and showed that their languages were related.",
  "Ceidwad Amgueddfa’r Ashmolean yn Rhydychen, a deithiodd Gymru, Cernyw, Llydaw, Iwerddon a’r Alban a dangos bod eu hieithoedd yn perthyn.","Edward_Lhuyd","william-morgan",
  "He collected fossils, plants, inscriptions and words, and the Snowdon lily is named Lloydia after him. His Archaeologia Britannica of 1707 laid the foundations for the study of these languages. It was this book that first put the name ‘Celtic’ on them; until then the Welsh had called themselves Britons and Cymry.",
  "Casglodd ffosilau, planhigion, arysgrifau a geiriau, ac enwir lili’r Wyddfa yn Lloydia ar ei ôl. Gosododd ei Archaeologia Britannica yn 1707 sylfeini astudio’r ieithoedd hyn. Y llyfr hwn a roddodd yr enw ‘Celtaidd’ arnynt gyntaf; hyd hynny, Brythoniaid a Chymry y galwai’r Cymry eu hunain."),
 ("ann-griffiths","industrial","1776–1805","Ann Griffiths","Ann Griffiths","Hymn writer","Emynyddes",
  "A farmer’s daughter from Dolwar Fach in Montgomeryshire whose few hymns are among the finest religious poetry in Welsh.",
  "Merch fferm o Ddolwar Fach yn Sir Drefaldwyn y mae ei hychydig emynau ymhlith y farddoniaeth grefyddol orau yn Gymraeg.","Ann_Griffiths","pantycelyn",
  "She never wrote her hymns down herself. Her maid, Ruth Evans, memorised them and recited them after Ann died at 29, soon after giving birth. Her hymn ‘Wele’n sefyll rhwng y myrtwydd’ is still widely sung.",
  "Ni ysgrifennodd ei hemynau ei hun erioed. Dysgodd ei morwyn, Ruth Evans, nhw ar ei chof a’u hadrodd ar ôl i Ann farw yn 29 oed, yn fuan ar ôl rhoi genedigaeth. Mae ei hemyn ‘Wele’n sefyll rhwng y myrtwydd’ yn dal i gael ei ganu’n eang."),
 ("mary-jones","industrial","1784–1864","Mary Jones","Mary Jones","The girl who walked for a Bible","Y ferch a gerddodd am Feibl",
  "A weaver’s daughter from Llanfihangel-y-Pennant who saved for six years to buy her own Welsh Bible.",
  "Merch gwehydd o Lanfihangel-y-Pennant a gynilodd am chwe blynedd i brynu ei Beibl Cymraeg ei hun.","Mary_Jones_(Bible)","jemima-nicholas",
  "In 1800 she walked to Bala to buy one from the preacher Thomas Charles. Her story helped persuade him and others to found the British and Foreign Bible Society in 1804. Her Bible is kept by the Bible Society in Cambridge.",
  "Yn 1800 cerddodd i’r Bala i brynu un gan y pregethwr Thomas Charles. Helpodd ei stori i’w ddarbwyllo ef ac eraill i sefydlu Cymdeithas y Beibl yn 1804. Cedwir ei Beibl gan Gymdeithas y Beibl yng Nghaergrawnt."),
 ("william-price","industrial","1800–1893","Dr William Price","Dr William Price","Rebel doctor of Llantrisant","Meddyg gwrthryfelgar Llantrisant",
  "A Chartist, druid and vegetarian doctor whose cremation of his baby son led to cremation becoming legal.",
  "Siartydd, derwydd a meddyg llysieuol yr arweiniodd ei amlosgiad o’i fab bach at gyfreithloni amlosgi.","William_Price_(physician)","betsi-cadwaladr",
  "He wore a fox-skin headdress and refused to treat patients who smoked. In 1884 he tried to cremate his son, named Iesu Grist, on a hill above Llantrisant. The court ruled cremation was not illegal, and his statue now stands in the town square.",
  "Gwisgai benwisg croen llwynog a gwrthodai drin cleifion a oedd yn ysmygu. Yn 1884 ceisiodd amlosgi ei fab, a enwyd yn Iesu Grist, ar fryn uwchben Llantrisant. Dyfarnodd y llys nad oedd amlosgi’n anghyfreithlon, ac mae ei gerflun yn sefyll heddiw ar sgwâr y dref."),
 ("michael-d-jones","industrial","1822–1898","Michael D. Jones","Michael D. Jones","Father of Y Wladfa","Tad y Wladfa",
  "A Bala minister who dreamed of a Welsh-speaking homeland overseas and led the plan to settle Patagonia.",
  "Gweinidog o’r Bala a freuddwydiodd am famwlad Gymraeg dros y môr ac a arweiniodd y cynllun i wladychu Patagonia.","Michael_D._Jones","henry-richard",
  "He had seen Welsh emigrants in America lose their language within a generation. He put much of his own money into the voyage of the Mimosa in 1865. He is often called the first modern Welsh nationalist.",
  "Roedd wedi gweld ymfudwyr o Gymru yn America’n colli’u hiaith o fewn cenhedlaeth. Rhoddodd lawer o’i arian ei hun tuag at fordaith y Mimosa yn 1865. Fe’i gelwir yn aml yn genedlaetholwr Cymreig modern cyntaf."),
 ("cranogwen","industrial","1839–1916","Cranogwen","Cranogwen","Sailor, poet and editor","Morwr, bardd a golygydd",
  "Sarah Jane Rees of Llangrannog, a master mariner’s teacher, prize-winning poet and editor of a Welsh magazine for women.",
  "Sarah Jane Rees o Langrannog, athrawes morwriaeth, bardd buddugol a golygydd cylchgrawn Cymraeg i fenywod.","Sarah_Jane_Rees","henry-richard",
  "She sailed with her father as a girl, earned a master’s certificate and taught navigation to young sailors. In 1865 she beat leading male poets at the National Eisteddfod. She edited Y Frythones and campaigned for temperance across Wales.",
  "Hwyliodd gyda’i thad yn ferch, enillodd dystysgrif meistr a dysgodd fordwyo i forwyr ifanc. Yn 1865 curodd brif feirdd gwrywaidd yr Eisteddfod Genedlaethol. Golygodd Y Frythones ac ymgyrchodd dros ddirwest ledled Cymru."),
 ("joseph-parry","industrial","1841–1903","Joseph Parry","Joseph Parry","Composer of ‘Myfanwy’","Cyfansoddwr ‘Myfanwy’",
  "A Merthyr boy who worked in the ironworks at ten and became the best-known Welsh composer of his age.",
  "Bachgen o Ferthyr a weithiodd yn y gwaith haearn yn ddeg oed ac a ddaeth yn gyfansoddwr Cymreig enwocaf ei oes.","Joseph_Parry","henry-richard",
  "His family emigrated to Pennsylvania, where he learned music. Chapel funds sent him to study in London, and he became professor of music at Aberystwyth. He wrote the hymn tune ‘Aberystwyth’, the song ‘Myfanwy’ and the first Welsh opera, ‘Blodwen’.",
  "Ymfudodd ei deulu i Bensylfania, lle dysgodd gerddoriaeth. Anfonodd arian y capeli ef i astudio yn Llundain, a daeth yn athro cerdd yn Aberystwyth. Ysgrifennodd y dôn emyn ‘Aberystwyth’, y gân ‘Myfanwy’ a’r opera Gymraeg gyntaf, ‘Blodwen’."),
 ("evan-roberts","industrial","1878–1951","Evan Roberts","Evan Roberts","Voice of the 1904 revival","Llais diwygiad 1904",
  "A former miner from Loughor whose preaching sparked the last great religious revival in Wales.",
  "Cyn-löwr o Gasllwchwr y taniodd ei bregethu’r diwygiad crefyddol mawr olaf yng Nghymru.","Evan_Roberts_(minister)","henry-richard",
  "In 1904 and 1905 he held meetings across south Wales, and around 100,000 people joined the chapels. Exhausted, he withdrew from public life and spent most of his remaining years quietly in Leicester and Cardiff.",
  "Yn 1904 a 1905 cynhaliodd gyfarfodydd ar draws de Cymru, ac ymunodd tua 100,000 o bobl â’r capeli. Wedi blino’n lân, tynnodd yn ôl o fywyd cyhoeddus a threuliodd y rhan fwyaf o’i flynyddoedd olaf yn dawel yng Nghaerlŷr a Chaerdydd."),
 ("hedd-wyn","modern","1887–1917","Hedd Wyn","Hedd Wyn","The poet of the black chair","Bardd y Gadair Ddu",
  "Ellis Humphrey Evans, a shepherd from Trawsfynydd, who won the eisteddfod chair weeks after he was killed in battle.",
  "Ellis Humphrey Evans, bugail o Drawsfynydd, a enillodd gadair yr eisteddfod wythnosau ar ôl iddo gael ei ladd mewn brwydr.","Hedd_Wyn","lloyd-george",
  "He was killed on the first day of the Battle of Passchendaele, 31 July 1917. His winning poem was ‘Yr Arwr’ (The Hero). His family farm, Yr Ysgwrn, is now open to visitors, with the black chair still in place.",
  "Fe’i lladdwyd ar ddiwrnod cyntaf Brwydr Passchendaele, 31 Gorffennaf 1917. Ei gerdd fuddugol oedd ‘Yr Arwr’. Mae fferm y teulu, Yr Ysgwrn, ar agor i ymwelwyr erbyn hyn, gyda’r gadair ddu yn dal yno."),
 ("kate-roberts","modern","1891–1985","Kate Roberts","Kate Roberts","Queen of Welsh prose","Brenhines ein llên",
  "A quarryman’s daughter from Rhosgadfan whose short stories and novels are the high point of modern Welsh prose.",
  "Merch chwarelwr o Rosgadfan y mae ei storïau byrion a’i nofelau’n uchafbwynt rhyddiaith Gymraeg fodern.","Kate_Roberts_(author)","saunders-lewis",
  "Her books, such as ‘Traed mewn Cyffion’ (Feet in Chains) and ‘Te yn y Grug’, show the hard, proud life of the slate villages. With her husband she ran the Gee press in Denbigh and its newspaper, Y Faner.",
  "Mae ei llyfrau, fel ‘Traed mewn Cyffion’ a ‘Te yn y Grug’, yn dangos bywyd caled a balch pentrefi’r llechi. Gyda’i gŵr rhedodd wasg Gee yn Ninbych a’i phapur newydd, Y Faner."),
 ("jim-griffiths","modern","1890–1975","Jim Griffiths","Jim Griffiths","First Secretary of State for Wales","Ysgrifennydd Gwladol cyntaf Cymru",
  "A miner from Betws near Ammanford who became a Labour minister and built the welfare state.",
  "Glöwr o’r Betws ger Rhydaman a ddaeth yn weinidog Llafur ac a adeiladodd y wladwriaeth les.","Jim_Griffiths","aneurin-bevan",
  "As Minister of National Insurance from 1945 he created the system of benefits for sickness, unemployment and old age. In 1964 he became the first Secretary of State for Wales.",
  "Fel Gweinidog Yswiriant Gwladol o 1945 creodd y drefn o fudd-daliadau ar gyfer salwch, diweithdra a henaint. Yn 1964 daeth yn Ysgrifennydd Gwladol cyntaf Cymru."),
 ("elaine-morgan","modern","1920–2013","Elaine Morgan","Elaine Morgan","Writer and thinker","Awdures a meddylwraig",
  "A miner’s daughter from Pontypridd who wrote award-winning television drama and popular books on human evolution.",
  "Merch glöwr o Bontypridd a ysgrifennodd ddrama deledu arobryn a llyfrau poblogaidd am esblygiad dyn.","Elaine_Morgan_(writer)","dylan-thomas",
  "Her book ‘The Descent of Woman’ challenged the male-centred science of the 1970s. She wrote a newspaper column into her nineties, and a statue of her was unveiled in Mountain Ash in 2022.",
  "Heriodd ei llyfr ‘The Descent of Woman’ wyddoniaeth wrywaidd y 1970au. Ysgrifennodd golofn papur newydd hyd ei nawdegau, a dadorchuddiwyd cerflun ohoni yn Aberpennar yn 2022."),
 ("r-s-thomas","modern","1913–2000","R. S. Thomas","R. S. Thomas","Poet and priest","Bardd ac offeiriad",
  "An Anglican priest in hill parishes and on Pen Llŷn, and one of the great poets in English of the 20th century.",
  "Offeiriad Anglicanaidd mewn plwyfi mynyddig ac ym Mhen Llŷn, ac un o feirdd Saesneg mawr yr ugeinfed ganrif.","R._S._Thomas","dylan-thomas",
  "His poems are spare and searching, about God, farmers and a Wales he feared was losing itself. He learned Welsh as an adult and wrote his prose autobiography in it. He was nominated for the Nobel Prize in Literature.",
  "Mae ei gerddi’n gynnil ac yn chwilgar, am Dduw, ffermwyr a Chymru yr ofnai ei bod yn colli’i hun. Dysgodd Gymraeg yn oedolyn ac ysgrifennodd ei hunangofiant rhyddiaith ynddi. Cafodd ei enwebu ar gyfer Gwobr Nobel am Lenyddiaeth."),
 ("richard-burton","modern","1925–1984","Richard Burton","Richard Burton","Actor with the golden voice","Actor â’r llais euraid",
  "Richard Jenkins, a miner’s son from Pontrhydyfen, who became one of the most famous film stars in the world.",
  "Richard Jenkins, mab glöwr o Bontrhydyfen, a ddaeth yn un o sêr ffilm enwocaf y byd.","Richard_Burton","dylan-thomas",
  "A teacher, Philip Burton, took him in and gave him his name. He was nominated for seven Oscars, and his reading of Dylan Thomas’s ‘Under Milk Wood’ is still famous. Welsh was his first language.",
  "Cymerodd athro, Philip Burton, ef dan ei adain a rhoi ei enw iddo. Cafodd ei enwebu am saith Oscar, ac mae ei ddarlleniad o ‘Under Milk Wood’ Dylan Thomas yn dal yn enwog. Cymraeg oedd ei iaith gyntaf."),
 ("betty-campbell","modern","1934–2017","Betty Campbell","Betty Campbell","Wales’s first Black head teacher","Pennaeth du cyntaf Cymru",
  "Raised in Butetown, Cardiff, she became head of Mount Stuart Primary and taught Black history long before it was common.",
  "Wedi’i magu yn Butetown, Caerdydd, daeth yn bennaeth Ysgol Gynradd Mount Stuart a dysgodd hanes pobl dduon ymhell cyn i hynny fod yn gyffredin.","Betty_Campbell","gwynfor-evans",
  "A teacher once told her that a Black girl from Butetown could not become a head teacher. She proved her wrong. In 2021 her statue in Cardiff became the first in Wales of a named, real woman to stand outdoors.",
  "Dywedodd athrawes wrthi unwaith na allai merch ddu o Butetown fod yn bennaeth. Profodd hi’n anghywir. Yn 2021 daeth ei cherflun yng Nghaerdydd yn gerflun awyr agored cyntaf Cymru o fenyw go iawn a enwir."),
 ("shirley-bassey","modern","born 1937","Shirley Bassey","Shirley Bassey","Tiger Bay’s great voice","Llais mawr Tiger Bay",
  "A singer from Tiger Bay in Cardiff, known around the world for three James Bond themes, including ‘Goldfinger’.",
  "Cantores o Tiger Bay yng Nghaerdydd, sy’n adnabyddus ar draws y byd am dair cân James Bond, gan gynnwys ‘Goldfinger’.","Shirley_Bassey","gwynfor-evans",
  "The youngest of seven children of a Nigerian father and an English mother, she left school at 14 and was singing in clubs by 16. Her career has lasted more than seventy years, and she was made a Dame in 2000.",
  "Yn ieuengaf o saith o blant tad o Nigeria a mam o Loegr, gadawodd yr ysgol yn 14 oed ac roedd yn canu mewn clybiau erbyn 16. Mae ei gyrfa wedi para dros saith deg mlynedd, a chafodd ei gwneud yn Fonesig yn 2000."),
 ("rhodri-morgan","modern","1939–2017","Rhodri Morgan","Rhodri Morgan","First Minister","Prif Weinidog",
  "First Minister of Wales from 2000 to 2009, who steered the young Assembly through its first decade.",
  "Prif Weinidog Cymru o 2000 i 2009, a lywiodd y Cynulliad ifanc drwy ei ddegawd cyntaf.","Rhodri_Morgan","gwynfor-evans",
  "He promised ‘clear red water’ between Wales and Westminster, bringing in free prescriptions and free bus travel for older people. Fluent in Welsh and famously informal, he was widely trusted across parties.",
  "Addawodd ‘ddŵr coch clir’ rhwng Cymru a San Steffan, gan gyflwyno presgripsiynau am ddim a theithio bws am ddim i bobl hŷn. Yn rhugl yn Gymraeg ac yn enwog o anffurfiol, roedd pleidiau o bob lliw’n ymddiried ynddo."),
 ("tanni-grey-thompson","modern","born 1969","Tanni Grey-Thompson","Tanni Grey-Thompson","Paralympic champion","Pencampwraig Baralympaidd",
  "A wheelchair racer from Cardiff who won eleven Paralympic gold medals and six London Marathons.",
  "Rasiwr cadair olwyn o Gaerdydd a enillodd un ar ddeg o fedalau aur Paralympaidd a chwe Marathon Llundain.","Tanni_Grey-Thompson","gwynfor-evans",
  "Born with spina bifida, she competed at five Paralympic Games from 1988 to 2004. She now sits in the House of Lords, where she speaks for disabled people.",
  "Fe’i ganed â spina bifida, a chystadlodd mewn pum Gêm Baralympaidd o 1988 i 2004. Mae’n eistedd yn Nhŷ’r Arglwyddi erbyn hyn, lle mae’n siarad dros bobl anabl."),
]

